Rose Agent @PROJECT_VERSION@ — bundled Qt @ROSE_PACKAGE_QT_VERSION@

The application's own licensing statement is in LICENSE. Bundled third-party
components retain their respective licenses; that statement does not override
the Qt or other third-party licenses.

This distribution dynamically links Qt Core, GUI, Widgets, Network, Concurrent,
Print Support, SVG and D-Bus, plus the platform, TLS, printer and image plugins.
Qt is Copyright (C) The Qt Company Ltd. and other contributors. This package
uses the LGPL-covered Qt components under their applicable GNU Lesser General
Public License version 3 terms, with exceptions and third-party notices as
supplied in the official Qt source. License texts and third-party attribution
files are installed beside this notice in qt/<module>/.

Corresponding official Qt source, including Qt's build instructions:
https://download.qt.io/archive/qt/@ROSE_PACKAGE_QT_SERIES@/@ROSE_PACKAGE_QT_VERSION@/single/qt-everywhere-src-@ROSE_PACKAGE_QT_VERSION@.tar.xz

The Qt shared libraries are installed in lib/rose-agent, outside the executable,
and are not statically linked into Rose Agent. You may replace these libraries
and plugins with compatible modified versions. No signature check prevents such
replacement. Reverse engineering to debug modifications to the LGPL-covered
libraries is permitted to the extent required by their applicable licenses.
The unmodified Qt runtime is deployed with a relative private runtime search
path; no application credential, configuration or user model file is shipped.

System libraries (including glibc, OpenSSL, X11/Wayland and font/rendering support)
are not bundled unless they are supplied as a dependency within the selected
Qt SDK itself. Notices and source provenance for such standalone SDK libraries
are in qt-sdk-dependencies/ when present. DEB and RPM packages declare
distribution-provided runtime libraries. See LinuxRuntimeDependencies.txt for
the ELF dependency list and package metadata for version constraints. The
portable archive also requires
those system runtime libraries, OpenSSL 3, xcb-cursor, CA certificates and fonts.

For application and release source information:
https://github.com/alertxsto/rose-agent
